index 29382fd9..e2ea4788 100644
--- a/compiler/v2/docs/core/compiler_core_roadmap_backlog.md
+++ b/compiler/v2/docs/core/compiler_core_roadmap_backlog.md
@@ -296,3 +296,27 @@ Goal: reduce repeated validation work before broad feature-catalog execution.
 | Optimization deferred | v2 artifact/string generation is not hot on the focused 2 KB baseline, so string-buffer rewrites, JSON-codec changes, and broader row aggregation changes remain deferred until a larger fixture or build-report timing row points there. |
 | O3 | Not run by design. |
 | Next-cycle note | If no-change build latency remains painful, instrument the Simple C++ build command around unaccounted orchestration/report-writing time and consider a compact/no-source-explanation mode for no-change builds before optimizing v2 artifact writers. |
+
+### Pre-Phase-9 Int64 Provider Binary-Plus Proof Report
+
+| Item | Result |
+|---|---|
+| Batch | F1 follow-up: narrow `int64` provider + binary-plus vertical proof |
+| Feature | Binary `+` over the existing `int64` primitive provider. |
+| Consumer row | `feature_binary_operator_plus_id()` through `CapabilityConsumerRow`; the fixture does not add a separate int64 feature path. |
+| Required contracts | Known TypeRef provider for `int64`, operation contract `binary_plus:int64_int64_to_int64`, inline scalar storage, trivial lifetime/copy/cleanup, and `primitive_i64_add` lowering adapter. |
+| Accepted minimal slice | Permanent fixture `compiler/v2/fixtures/int64_local_return` with `$x int64 = 40; return $x + 2;`. |
+| Implementation | The PHS frontend now threads the declared return TypeRef into return expression rows and retags typed local variable/initializer rows from local declaration syntax. The focused runner now asserts that `int64_local_return` emits nonzero lowering and LLVM text and that the generated LLVM contains `alloca i64`, `store i64 40`, `add i64`, and `ret i64`. |
+| Tokenizer coverage | Covered by the existing tokenizer path. Focused run saw 21 tokens and zero parser errors; no tokenizer change was needed. |
+| Parser coverage | Covered by `frontend_model_builder.phs`: `int64` remains parsed through generic identifier type syntax, now preserved on local and return expression TypeRefs. |
+| Lowering coverage | Covered by focused compiled fixture run: 3 backend requests and 3 lowering steps for the int64 local-store/load-plus-return path. |
+| LLVM/text sink coverage | Covered by focused compiled fixture run: 549 LLVM text bytes, with i64 local storage, load, `add i64`, and i64 return. |
+| Permanent tests | `int64_local_return` remains in the permanent bootstrap full fixture set; `run_fixture_focus.sh` now has fixture-specific int64 assertions for cheap edit-time proof. |
+| Benchmark protocol | Standard protocol is `SCPP_V2_FOCUS_FIXTURE_KEYS=int64_local_return SCPP_SKIP_COMPILER_BUILD=1 bash compiler/v2/run_fixture_focus.sh`; broader smoke/incremental/full gate stays `SCPP_SKIP_COMPILER_BUILD=1 bash compiler/v2/run_readiness_gate.sh` after one compiler build. Scaling, benchmark, and O3 are opt-in only. |
+| Performance measurement | Focused int64 run reported 1 ms compiler-side elapsed, with tokenizer/parser/frontend/symbol/backend profile rows present. The compiler rebuild after PHS edits remains the real cost: one failed build exposed a stale incremental helper call after 113.7 s; the corrected resumed debug build took 548.5 s. |
+| Incremental added/changed/removed coverage | Covered at the batch-gate level by `run_incremental_proof.sh`. Int64-specific added/changed/removed source variants remain debt until resident local body parse slices carry the owning symbol return TypeRef instead of the current neutral/default expected return TypeRef. |
+| Multithreading coverage | Debt. No worker execution exists yet. The touched rows remain per-source/per-function owned and deterministic; no shared mutable global state or cross-partition ordering dependency was added. |
+| Implementation performance review | No speculative string/buffer rewrite was added. The hot cost observed here is still compiler rebuild fanout, not int64 fixture execution or LLVM text materialization. The implementation adds one compact expression-payload update helper and passes TypeRef ids through existing rows. |
+| Concrete type branches | Adapter-local only: `int64` selects the existing primitive i64 LLVM add path through provider/consumer/contract rows. No duplicated binary-plus feature implementation was added. |
+| Validation | `bash -n compiler/v2/run_fixture_focus.sh`; `git diff --check`; fresh debug compiler rebuild after fixing one stale helper call; focused `int64_local_return`; `SCPP_SKIP_COMPILER_BUILD=1 bash compiler/v2/run_readiness_gate.sh` in 8.3 s. |
+| O3 | Not run by design; this was a debug-path provider proof, not an O3 performance claim. |
